[center][size=6][b]FIND[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#e8c882]B A S E   S T O R A G E   S E A R C H[/color][/size]

[size=3]Where did I put the Shroud Liquid? Press Shift+F and the chest lights up.[/size][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609966-1205231011.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

Stand in your base and press [b]Shift+F[/b]. A search box opens, drawn with the game's own dialog, so it looks like part of Enshrouded. Type what you are looking for:
[list]
[*][b]Suggestions as you type[/b], each with how many you have and in how many chests: [i]Granite Block — 996 in 1 chest[/i].
[*][b]Pick with Tab, the arrow keys or the mouse.[/b] The mouse wheel scrolls long lists. [b]Enter[/b] finds.
[*][b]The matching chests pulse[/b] with the game's own highlight, so you can walk straight to them.
[*][b]Open one and the items you searched for glow gold[/b] for a few seconds, every matching slot, so you see them at once in a full chest.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609967-2012517538.png[/img]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609972-219583874.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What you can search for[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609387-300384686.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Items[/b], by the name the game shows. Partial words work: [i]stone[/i] finds Stone and Rough Stone Block.
[*][b]Kinds of items[/b]: categories ([i]Consumables[/i], [i]Ammunition[/i]...), rarities ([i]Uncommon[/i] to [i]Legendary[/i]), item types ([i]One-Handed Axe[/i]...) and perks ([i]Backstab Damage[/i]...). They are labelled in the list, like [i]Perk: Backstab Damage — 12 items in 3 chests[/i].
[*][b]Chest names you gave yourself[/b] with Rename. (The game's own "Storage Chest" titles are not searched, as every unnamed chest would match.)
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\find[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game, stand inside one of your bases and press [b]Shift+F[/b].
[/list]

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Updating from 1.0.x:[/b] delete [i]wsock32.dll[/i] from the game folder. Your [i]find.ini[/i] moves to [i]greeneye\find\[/i] by itself.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\find[/i]; if no other Greeneye mod is left, also [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[i]greeneye\find\find.ini[/i] is written on the first start. Restart the game after changing it.
[list]
[*][b]hotkey[/b] = Shift+F: the key that opens the search, for example [i]Ctrl+F[/i] or [i]F6[/i].
[*][b]glow_seconds[/b] = 180: the found chests glow at most this long (10-3600), or until your next search.
[*][b]near_meters[/b] = 2.5: coming this close to a found chest counts as reaching it (0.5-20).
[*][b]near_seconds[/b] = 3: a chest stops glowing this long after you reach or open it (0-60).
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Your language[/b][/size]

Find follows the language set in the game. Item, perk, category and rarity names are the game's own. Find's few texts of its own come in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Polish, Russian, Ukrainian, Japanese, Korean, Chinese and Turkish. (Corrections from native speakers are welcome.)

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Client-side only.[/b] Servers need nothing installed, and other players do not need the mod.
[*][b]Only reads your chests.[/b] It never moves, adds or removes an item.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Quick Deposit, Continue and Auto Loot), and where another mod such as Creative Mode hooks the same game function, Find chains onto its hook.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. After an update the mod checks that it still recognises the game; if it does not, it switches itself off (and says so in [i]find.log[/i]) instead of risking a crash.
[*]Opens only while you play or have your backpack open, never while you type in chat, rename something or write on a signpost.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Searches the chests of the base you stand in, not all your bases at once.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post these two files from the game folder with your report:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\find\find.log[/i]: what Find did.
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i]: what the Greeneye Loader did.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]1.1.7[/b]
[list]
[*]Switching to another world without restarting the game no longer makes Find say "This base has no storage chests to search" in a base full of chests (a 1.1.6 bug).
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]No storage chests found after switching worlds.
[/list]

[b]1.1.6[/b]
[list]
[*]Planted bushes are no longer treated as chests. The flame altar counts their fruit toward crafting, so searching "hazelnut" lit up every Hazelnut bush in the base, and with many of them in view the game crashed.
[*]Crafting stations (spinning wheel, kiln, tanning station and the like) are no longer listed as chests in a base that has planted bushes.
[*]Through-wall chest outlines have a detail limit, so many outlines at once can no longer crash the game.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Game crash right after searching "hazelnut" (reported by Lomack).
[/list]

[b]1.1.5[/b]
[list]
[*]Works in a base whose altar lists no chests (a small flame altar): Find searches the storage chests inside the base instead of saying it has none.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]"This base has no storage chests to search" with a chest in the base (reported by Andydark287).
[/list]

[b]1.1.4[/b]
[list]
[*]An NPC's Summoning Staff is found as "Summoning Staff" too: the game names it after the NPC ("Fenrig Mills, Jr."), so only the NPC's name found it. Find lists it as "Summoning Staff (Fenrig Mills, Jr.)".
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Searching "summon" did not find Summoning Staffs (reported by HadToRegister).
[/list]

[b]1.1.3[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed: in some bases a search missed items past a chest's first row and every chest not linked to the flame altar ("purple" found nothing although Purple Berries were in a chest). It happened when the base's first chest had only one row.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Search did not find Purple Berries stored in the base.
[/list]

[b]1.1.2[/b]
[list]
[*]Works alongside the XHL mods (Vein Mining, Area Harvest, Free Climbing and the others): with Find installed, their F10 settings menu was missing and Area Harvest did not start. Find now hooks only its own calls to the game functions they look up, never the functions themselves.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]XHL mods (Vein Mining, Auto Harvest) stopped working and their F10 menu was missing with Find installed (reported by HadToRegister).
[/list]

[b]1.1.1[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed: in a base where your game had not loaded the base's first chest yet (a large base, often on a server), every search found nothing. Find now tries every chest of the base, then your own backpack.
[*]Fixed: after switching worlds without restarting the game (your own world, then a server), Find searched the old world and found nothing.
[/list]

[b]1.1.0[/b]
[list]
[*]Runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i]), shared with Quick Deposit, Continue and Auto Loot. [i]find.ini[/i] and [i]find.log[/i] now live in [i]greeneye\find\[/i].
[*]New settings in [i]find.ini[/i]: [b]glow_seconds[/b] (how long chests glow at most), [b]near_meters[/b] (how close counts as reaching a chest) and [b]near_seconds[/b] (how long a chest keeps glowing after you reach or open it). Raise near_seconds to keep chests lit while you walk between them.
[*]Found chests glow at most three minutes by default (was five).
[*]The found items inside a chest glow only the first time you open it.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed and requests:
[list]
[*]Items glowed again every time a chest was reopened (reported by Dacrenzio).
[*]Chests should stay highlighted longer (requested by HadToRegister).
[/list]

[b]1.0.2[/b]
[list]
[*]Works with Creative Mode: 1.0.1 switched itself off next to it ("signature not found: LocaText"); Find now finds the game functions Creative Mode hooks and chains onto its hooks.
[*]Finds a game function another mod has already hooked by the code behind that hook, so load order between mods matters less.
[*]Inside a base without storage chests, Find says "This base has no storage chests to search." instead of claiming you are not in a base.
[*]Outside a base the search field is switched off; Enter or Esc closes it.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Find inactive next to Creative Mode (reported by Dacrenzio, cnrat and Bigdaddy2I42).
[*]"Not in a base" shown in a base that has no storage chests (reported by GreeneyeDS).
[/list]

[b]1.0.1[/b]
[list]
[*]Esc hands the keyboard back to the game.
[/list]

[b]1.0.0[/b]
[list]
[*]First release.
[/list]

